ia, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Motaparthi K", "lastName": "Motaparthi", "firstName": "Kiran", "initials": "K", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0562-0826"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Dermatology, University of Florida College of Medicine, Gainesville, Florida, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Cockerell CJ", "lastName": "Cockerell", "firstName": "Clay J", "initials": "CJ", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Cockerell Dermatopathology, Dallas, Texas, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Feeser TA", "lastName": "Feeser", "firstName": "Theresa A", "initials": "TA", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Proscia Inc., Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lee JB", "lastName": "Lee", "firstName": "Jason B", "initials": "JB", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Departments of Dermatology and Cutaneous Biology, Sidney Kimmel Medical College at Thomas Jefferson University, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2579-1510"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0562-0826"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "10", "journalIssueId": 2908367, "dateOfPublication": "2020 Feb", "monthOfPublication": 2, "yearOfPublication": 2020, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Sci Rep", "title": "Scientific reports", "essn": "2045-2322", "issn": "2045-2322", "nlmid": "101563288", "isoabbreviation": "Sci Rep"}, "printPublicationDate": "2020-02-01"}, "pubYear": "2020", "pageInfo": "3217", "abstractText": "Standard of care diagnostic procedure for suspected skin cancer is microscopic examination of hematoxylin & eosin stained tissue by a pathologist. Areas of high inter-pathologist discordance and rising biopsy rates necessitate higher efficiency and diagnostic reproducibility. We present and validate a deep learning system which classifies digitized dermatopathology slides into 4 categories. The system is developed using 5,070 images from a single lab, and tested on an uncurated set of 13,537 images from 3 test labs, using whole slide scanners manufactured by 3 different vendors. The system's use of deep-learning-based confidence scoring as a criterion to consider the result as accurate yields an accuracy of up to 98%, and makes it adoptable in a real-world setting. Without confidence scoring, the system achieved an accuracy of 78%. We anticipate that our deep learning system will serve as a foundation enabling faster diagnosis of skin cancer, identification of cases for specialist review, and targeted diagnostic classifications.", "affiliation": "Proscia Inc., Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA. julianna@proscia.com.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Melanocytes", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CY", "qualifierName": "cytology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Skin Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Image Interpretation, Computer-Assisted", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Calibration"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Prospective Studies"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Reproducibility of Results"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "ROC Curve"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Pathology", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": 